WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:08.794
Now we set up the exam itself: Periodic Test 1, October 2026, for Class 10, Section A.

00:00:09.544 --> 00:00:12.494
Open Exams from the menu and choose New exam.

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:17.188
Type the exam's name, and choose its kind: Unit test.

00:00:17.894 --> 00:00:24.160
The session and term are filled in for you. The grading scheme is the default we made: Class 10 grading.

00:00:26.385 --> 00:00:31.741
Tick the section that sits this exam: Class 10, Section A. Then create the exam.

00:00:33.683 --> 00:00:40.158
The exam starts as a draft. This list shows what is still needed before teachers can enter marks.

00:00:41.221 --> 00:00:45.658
Each subject is a paper. Add paper, and choose Mathematics.

00:00:46.852 --> 00:00:54.350
A paper is made of components. Choose the Internal 40 plus External 60 preset, and rename External to Written.

00:00:58.134 --> 00:01:04.215
The paper is out of 100. The pass mark comes from the grading scheme: 33 percent.

00:01:05.124 --> 00:01:11.093
Add the other four subjects the same way: Science, English, Hindi and Social Science.

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:19.171
Now assign the teacher. From the Mathematics paper's menu, choose Assign faculty, tick Amit Kumar, and save.

00:01:20.165 --> 00:01:26.304
Everything is ready. Open marks entry, and teachers can start entering marks for their papers.

00:01:27.142 --> 00:01:33.871
Papers can still be added while entry is open. Next, Mr. Amit Kumar enters the Mathematics marks.
